# OI + FLOW BUILD_CONT

Research project focused on continuation setups in Binance Futures based on the interaction between price shocks, Open Interest expansion, and aggressive taker flow.

## Overview

This project explored whether abnormal price moves combined with Open Interest growth and taker order flow could indicate continuation rather than mean reversion.

## Research Scope

- Historical market data processing
- Open Interest analysis
- Taker flow analysis
- Automated signal generation
- Out-of-sample backtesting
- Transaction cost modeling
- Execution delay testing
- Risk and performance analysis
- Shadow monitoring of live market conditions

## Findings

Under historical out-of-sample testing with transaction costs and execution delays modeled, the approach retained positive performance characteristics.

## Purpose

The objective was to test whether positioning and flow data could be structured into a measurable continuation signal under realistic execution assumptions.

> This project is intended for research and educational purposes only.
